       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 8000 mg per dose four times daily is 32,000 mg/day, which is about 10 times the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, given as 800 mg per dose four times daily. A dose of 8000 mg could cause serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean **800 mg by mouth four times daily**? That would be 3,200 mg/day, the maximum for an adult. Many clinicians start lower, for example 400\u2013600 mg every 6\u20138 hours, and give it with food.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose you want, I'll enter it right away. If 8000 mg is what you intended, tell me the clinical reason and I'll note it on the order. I'd still advise confirming it with pharmacy first."
